# Copy to .env in this project (it is gitignored), or set these as real environment
# variables. Everything here is optional: with no keys at all, reading, the vocabulary
# measurement and spaced repetition still work.
#
# Every line is commented out on purpose. Uncomment what you need -- the app tells you
# in Settings what is configured and what is missing, and that panel writes to
# data/settings.json, which takes precedence over this file anyway.

# --- Graded exercises (optional) --------------------------------------------
# TypeSafe System One. Returns a judgment with a confidence, which is what
# translation grading needs. Get a key at https://console.typesafe.ai/keys
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=apikey_...
# TYPESAFE_MODEL=jev-latest

# --- Tutor (optional, and the one that matters) ------------------------------
# Any OpenAI-compatible chat completions endpoint. Used for word glosses,
# comprehension questions, translation drills, and weaving imported articles.
# TYPESAFE above is the grader; this is the writer. Without it the app still reads
# and reviews, and says so rather than failing.
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com/provider/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=...
# LLM_MODEL=the-model-name-your-endpoint-expects

# --- Options ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the hand-made diglot corpus lives. Defaults to ./corpus inside the project.
# DIGLOT_CORPUS=/path/to/your/own/diglot/articles

# Where the database and imported articles go. Defaults to ./data.
# DIGLOT_DATA=./data

# Only if this machine reaches the web through a proxy (import and discovery).
# Empty or absent means connect directly, which is what almost every machine wants.
# DIGLOT_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:7890
